      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.85,
      "end_seconds": 5.87,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "good evening, you know, doctor, thanks for seeing me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.68,
      "end_seconds": 10.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.52,
      "end_seconds": 30.25,
      "duration_seconds": 17.73,
      "text": "oh um so the thing is I've got a severe sore throat on one side it's the not knowing that gets to me i told myself I'd wait and see and here I am"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.18,
      "end_seconds": 35.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "alright, what aggravates it, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.96,
      "end_seconds": 40.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "I I notice it more with swallowing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.91,
      "end_seconds": 50.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "What about difficulty opening your mouth, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.01,
      "end_seconds": 56.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Yes, actually. About difficulty opening my mouth, mostly moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.55,
      "end_seconds": 62.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "What about a muffled voice have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.92,
      "end_seconds": 70.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "yes, since last night about muffled voice, about a four out of ten"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.05,
      "end_seconds": 76.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "have you noticed cough, noisy breathing or rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.98,
      "end_seconds": 81.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "No cough noisy breathing or rash none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.24,
      "end_seconds": 87.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "what about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.18,
      "end_seconds": 92.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.31,
      "end_seconds": 106.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.68,
      "end_seconds": 111.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "it's amlodipine 5 milligrams once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.32,
      "end_seconds": 115.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "alright is that long-standing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.8,
      "end_seconds": 117.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "About a month now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.4,
      "end_seconds": 120.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.46,
      "end_seconds": 131.67,
      "duration_seconds": 9.21,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, yes, I had my womb taken out, fifteen years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.37,
      "end_seconds": 136.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.58,
      "end_seconds": 141.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "my uncle has high cholesterol"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.05,
      "end_seconds": 145.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Before we go further any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.68,
      "end_seconds": 148.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "no allergies at all"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.71,
      "end_seconds": 160.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.42,
      "end_seconds": 164.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.47,
      "end_seconds": 178.44,
      "duration_seconds": 11.97,
      "text": "right, so high blood pressure is already on your record we'll keep that in mind today tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.3,
      "end_seconds": 192.02,
      "duration_seconds": 12.72,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.1,
      "end_seconds": 196.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.83,
      "end_seconds": 205.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "keep your arm relaxed for me.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.87,
      "end_seconds": 228.4,
      "duration_seconds": 8.53,
      "text": "okay: temperature 39.1, pulse is 107 beats a minute, saturation 97 percent and blood pressure 121 over 66."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.67,
      "end_seconds": 234.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "could you come over to the couch please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.33,
      "end_seconds": 236.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "breathe out slowly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.57,
      "end_seconds": 258.94,
      "duration_seconds": 7.37,
      "text": "The right tonsil is pushed towards the middle, the uvula is deviated, and the palate is swollen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.87,
      "end_seconds": 280.3,
      "duration_seconds": 17.43,
      "text": "thank you you can get dressed. Let me tell you where I've got to. It's hard to say. A quinsy, a peritonsillar abscess is one possibility and severe tonsillitis another and I'd rather not commit yet"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.93,
      "end_seconds": 314.93,
      "duration_seconds": 18.0,
      "text": "We should do blood tests for abscess. I'm prescribing benzylpenicillin 1.2 grams now single dose. That should help with peritonsillar abscess. You need to be seen by ENT today to drain it. Please come and see me straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.46,
      "end_seconds": 323.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "I'll book it it on my way out"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.71,
      "end_seconds": 327.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.54,
      "end_seconds": 332.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "no uh that's all. Thanks a lot"
    }
  ]
